airconv, dxmt, d3d11: Bound constant-buffer reads.

Games read past a constant buffer's declared size, which D3D11 allows and
Apple GPUs fault on. Each buffer's bound length goes into the argument
buffer beside its address and shaders clamp the index before loading, so an
out-of-range read returns zero. D3D11.1 ranges are honoured. The shader
cache version moves to 19 for the new argument layout.
